    {
      "sentence_id": 1,
      "japanese": "昔々、山の中に小さな村がありました。",
      "english_translation": "Once upon a time, there was a small village nestled in the mountains."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 2,
      "japanese": "その村には、ケンという男が住んでいました。",
      "english_translation": "There was a man named Ken living in that village."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 3,
      "japanese": "ケンはいつも静かで、よく一人で森に行き、変わった石を集めるのが好きでした。",
      "english_translation": "Ken was always quiet, and he often went into the forest alone, enjoying collecting unusual stones."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 4,
      "japanese": "村の人たちは「どうしてそんな石を集めるの？」と聞きましたが、ケンは「ただ好きだから」とだけ答えていました。",
      "english_translation": "The villagers asked, \"Why do you collect so many stones?\" But Ken simply replied, \"I just like them.\""
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 5,
      "japanese": "ある日、ケンが森を歩いていると、今まで見たことがない、とても大きくて光る石を見つけました。",
      "english_translation": "One day, Ken was walking through the forest when he came across a very large and luminous stone that he had never seen before."
    }
